From 91e5bef8b46a7c872fbb724bcd164c4a23f9c6e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aquarat <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 19:29:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [RFC] arm64: dts: apple: t8103: mark the AVD as dma-coherent

Without dma-coherent the AVD's V4L2 buffers are mapped Normal-NC, and
reading decoded frames back through that mapping runs at ~250 MB/s on
the M1 (one serialised uncached transaction per load), i.e. ~18 ms of
CPU per 2304x1296 NV12 frame for any client that copies frames to
system memory (ffmpeg v4l2request -> swscale, GStreamer videoconvert).

Testing suggests the decoder's DMA is coherent with the CPU caches on
the T8103. With the driver forcing dev->dma_coherent = true (which is
exactly what this property does for a device behind a DART: cacheable
dma_alloc mappings, no dma_sync maintenance), an instrumented driver
pulled the first 2 MiB of every destination buffer into the caches
right before starting the decode and compared, on the same CPU after
the decode-done interrupt, the cached view with the contents after
"dc civac": 0 stale lines in 450 frames (3 x 150-frame 2304x1296 High
CABAC decodes), and every decode was bit-identical to software decode
per frame. The driver's own CPU-written instruction and firmware
buffers were cacheable in the same test and the decoder consumed them
correctly, so device reads are coherent as well.

With the property the read-back costs the same as a memcpy from RAM
(~20 GB/s) for every client and without any cache maintenance:
ffmpeg -hwaccel v4l2request 2304x1296, 150 frames, decode + copy to
system memory: 2.75 s user -> 0.08 s user + 0.03 s sys (the
non-coherent/allow_cache_hints alternative in the driver gives 0.08 s
user + 0.12 s sys because videobuf2 cleans and invalidates the 13 MB
planes on every buffer).

Marked RFC: the coherency was established empirically on one T8103,
not from documentation. It should be confirmed (and checked for the
T6000/T8112 AVDs) before this is merged; the same result was not
verified with a rebuilt DTB, only with the equivalent driver-side
override.

Signed-off-by: <fill in>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi
index dfb5f73..63f8bd8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8103.dtsi
@@ -1419,6 +1419,7 @@
 				<0x2 0x69100000 0x0 0x10000>;
 			reg-names = "code", "sram", "mbox", "ctrl";
 			iommus = <&avd_dart 0>;
+			dma-coherent;
 		};
 
 		avd_dart: iommu@269010000 {
